<%# locals: () %>
<%# The LIST's head, and it lives inside the list column - not across the page.
    A head reaches as far as the thing it belongs to: rendered above the grid it
    spanned both columns, so "7 Spalten" stood over the detail lane although it
    is the list that has columns. In the column it also stops pushing the lane
    down, and the lane starts at the top of the content area where the object
    belongs, beside the page title rather than under the toolbar.

    Order left to right: which view -> how narrowed -> which columns. Tools sit
    right behind the tabs, not flush right: flush right they wander with the
    content width and end up over the detail. The right end stays free for what
    is fleeting - a selection count, a draft state. %>
<%# ⚠️ The page title lives HERE, inside the list column, and not across the
    page. It names what the column holds - a list of tickets in this project -
    and while it stood above the grid the lane could not reach the top of the
    content area: the lane began under the title instead of beside it. The
    object's identifier and the page title now share a height, which is the
    hierarchy the detail head was rebuilt for (page top left, object one step
    lower and to the right).
    It carries what belongs to the page: help, and the main action that creates
    a ticket in this very list. %>
<%= render NeoProjectLayoutHeaderComponent.new(
  title: t('views.organisations.tickets.index.title'),
  subtitle: @project.name,
  project: @project,
  active_smart_folder: @active_smart_folder,
  selected_item: @selected_ticket,
  content_open: @open_content,
  context_type: :tickets,
  view_mode: @view_mode || 'table',
  # One rhythm down this column: 14px from the page title to the list head, and
  # the same 14px from the head to the column labels (the bar's own mb-3.5).
  # The page-wide mb-6 was a title standing above a page; this one stands on
  # the head of its own list.
  margin_bottom: 'mb-3.5'
) do |header| %>
  <% header.with_right_content do %>
    <%# The page header carries what belongs to the PAGE: the view switch, help
        and the main action.
        ⚠️ "Liste | Kanban" is a PAGE element, not a list tool (designer,
        07.09.2026). It decides whether there is a table at all - in kanban
        there are no columns and no detail lane - so it stands with the title
        and not among the three that narrow the list down. It spent one day in
        the tab row on the opposite argument ("a control belongs with the thing
        it changes"); the thing it changes turned out to be the page.
        Stands at every state, with a ticket open too (user, 09.09.2026): both
        views open the ticket in the same lane, and update_view_mode redirects
        back to the live address with the ticket_id, so the switch keeps the
        ticket in both directions and only swaps what one picks from
        (doc/kanban_ticket_als_bahn_plan.md, rule 7). It used to step aside
        while the lane was open on the table, from the days the board had no
        lane. %>
    <div class="flex items-center">

    <% unless @view_mode == 'kanban' && @kanban_columns.nil? %>
      <div class="me-2.5 flex items-center" data-page-view-switch>
        <%# The icon pair (designer, 09.09.2026): the groove with its word
            labels was the largest element of the row, four signals for one
            statement, on a control that is used seldom. The caption is
            mandatory, the kanban sign is not self-explaining: title,
            aria-label and the keyboard tooltip carry the word. One
            definition for every view switch: NeoViewSwitchComponent. %>
        <%= render NeoViewSwitchComponent.new(
          label: t('kanban.view_mode_label'),
          variant: :icon_pair,
          container_class: 'hidden sm:inline-flex',
          items: %w[table kanban].map do |mode|
            { key: mode.to_sym, icon: (mode == 'table' ? :list : :kanban), title: t("kanban.view_mode_#{mode}"),
              active: (@view_mode || 'table') == mode,
              path: update_view_mode_organisation_project_view_configuration_path(@current_organisation, @project),
              method: :patch, params: { view_mode: mode },
              disabled: mode == 'kanban' && @view_configuration&.resolved_kanban_attribute.nil? }
          end
        ) %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
    <%= render 'common/contextual_help_menu', context: :tickets %>

    <%# Settings dropdown removed: View Settings opens via the gear in the table header;
        Detail Settings via the action bar in the detail panel; manage ticket fields via
        project settings (edit project page). Modal markup remains below. %>

    <%# Detail Settings Modal — shared between action bar and settings dropdown %>
    <% detail_show_time = policy(@project).area_access?(:time_sessions, :read) rescue false %>
    <%= render 'organisations/tickets/detail_settings_modal',
               current_organisation: @current_organisation,
               project: @project,
               view_config: @view_configuration,
               show_time: detail_show_time,
               hide_trigger: true %>

    <%# The clock button and its capture modal are gone (designer handoff
        "Uebergabe Tickets" §9): a timer icon up here had no visible object.
        Capturing time happens at the hours sum in the ticket header
        (SubjectTimeSummaryComponent -> capture popover); capturing without a
        ticket stays on the times list, where the context really is missing. %>
    </div>

    <% if policy(@project).area_access?(:tickets, :write) %>
      <%# The main action sits outermost (user, 04.09.2026). Opens the
          viewport-filling writing surface into turbo-frame#writing_surface (Paket 3). %>
      <%= render Neo::Buttons::IconButtonComponent.new(
        variant: :primary,
        icon: "plus-lg",
        size: :medium,
        tag: :a,
        href: new_organisation_project_ticket_path(@current_organisation, @project, source: 'index_page'),
        title: t('views.organisations.tickets.index.new_task_tooltip'),
        # 3 px of air to the right: the list column clips at its edge
        # (overflow auto), and the main action's offset shadow needs the room.
        class: "ml-3 me-[3px]",
        data: { turbo_frame: "writing_surface" }
      ) %>
    <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<%# Unified Filter Bar: SmartFolder pills + Ad-hoc Filters + Search.
    Hidden on first use (no tickets at all — style guide "Leerzustände"):
    filters over nothing only add noise. Reappears with the next full page
    load after the first ticket exists. %>
<% unless tickets_first_use?(@project) %>
<%= render NeoFilterBarComponent.new(
  current_user_id: current_user&.id,
  smart_folders: @ticket_smart_folders,
  url: organisation_project_tickets_path(@current_organisation, @project),
  frame_id: 'tickets_list_frame',
  i18n_scope: 'views.organisations.tickets.index',
  all_items_label: t('smart_folders.all_tickets', default: 'Alle Tickets'),
  smart_folder_context_type: 'Ticket',
  smart_folder_return_to: 'tickets',
  active_smart_folder: @active_smart_folder,
  active_view_permissions: filter_bar_view_permissions(@active_smart_folder),
  dissolver_result: @dissolver_result,
  ad_hoc_filters: ad_hoc_filter_params.presence || {},
  ad_hoc_operators: ad_hoc_filter_op_params.presence || {},
  dropped_categories: dropped_filter_categories,
  filter_categories_json: ad_hoc_filter_categories_json(@project),
  search_value: params[:search],
  search_mode: @current_search_mode,
  project: @project,
  organisation: @current_organisation
) do |bar| %>
  <%# The column picker's trigger (F39) lives in the bar since 20a (S2):
      columns belong to the view, like the conditions do. In the table header
      it held a column's width and never showed a value in it.
      ⚠️ A SIGN, at every width, and no count beside it (user, 07.09.2026): the
      right end of a narrow head holds the search and this, and nothing else.
      It used to carry "6 Spalten", which a width rule then had to take away
      again - a label that only fits sometimes is a label that has to be
      managed. The number is in the title, where the whole sentence fits. %>
  <% bar.with_selection_row do %>
    <%= render 'organisations/tickets/selection_row' %>
  <% end %>
  <%# Not on the board (D5 of doc/kanban_ticket_als_bahn_plan.md): the picker
      chooses the TABLE's columns, and it rendered on the board with nothing
      behind it. %>
  <% if @view_mode != 'kanban' %>
  <% bar.with_view_tool do %>
    <button type="button"
            class="column-picker-trigger grid place-items-center h-7 w-7 rounded-md text-muted
                   hover:text-heading hover:bg-cream-100 transition-colors
                   focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ink"
            data-column-picker-trigger
            data-action="click->column-picker#toggle"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="<%= Neo::ColumnPickerComponent::ELEMENT_ID %>"
            title="<%= t('components.column_picker.trigger_title') %>">
      <i class="bi bi-sliders2 text-sm" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <%# A sign, and nothing beside it (user, 07.09.2026). It carried a count
          and then a word; both said something the table next to it already
          shows. The caption lives in the title ("Spalten wählen"), which is
          also what a screen reader announces - a sign is never left without
          one, it just does not have to be read every time. No number in it
          either (designer, 09.09.2026): the chosen columns stand as heads
          below and in the panel itself. 28 x 28 like the two tools beside it. %>
    </button>
  <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
<% end %>
